    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The Moomins are fairy-tale characters created by the Finland-Swedish author and illustrator Tove Jansson. They first appeared in 1945 in the novel The Moomins and the Great Flood, and by 1993 the series comprised nine novels, five picture books and one comic strip. The books have been translated into 55 languages, with combined sales of more than 30 million copies. With their rounded figures, the Moomins are often mistaken for hippos, but they are in fact Finnish forest sprites from Nordic folklore. Kind-hearted, helpful and brave, they live with their family in Moominvalley, surrounded by mountains, and love to explore and embark on adventures — often stumbling into all manner of strange and wonderful happenings.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "text": null,
      "url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/fzk67ae/412fcd6566a5b7ae.jpg",
      "full_url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/fzk67ae/2018ccaf98def9da.jpg",
