    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "This group of bags features Moomin comic strips by Tove Jansson as its main visual motif. The strip was first serialized in 1954 in the London Evening News, told in four-panel black-and-white installments per page with lively, witty dialogue, chronicling the humorous everyday life and adventures of the Moomin family and their friends in Moominvalley. The large Pinacoteca bag is reversible: one side is pure white Intrecciato woven leather, while the other is printed with the black-and-white comic artwork. Long and compact zip-around wallets complete the lineup.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
